# L §7.2 rounds a `num U`; L §3.3 "A rate is not money and not a bare number" and enters arithmetic only through
# its built-ins: `round` of a rate has no meaning, LOAD-UNIT at load (L §8.4).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input r: rate
def c: rate = round(r, 1, half-up) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 5 %/year

ask q: c law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT ...
